# Test: ze doctor --json reports a PPPoE config the host's kernel cannot carry
# VALIDATES: the pppoe kernel capability enrolment (CONFIG_PPPOE, the PPPoX
# discovery socket) is reachable from the USER entry point. A forced absent
# answer is an ERROR, so `ze doctor` exits 1 and the message names the kernel
# feature and the configuration that asked.
# PREVENTS: a PPPoE access concentrator that accepts a configuration on a kernel
# with no PPPoE and answers no subscriber. This replaces doctor-pppoe-module.ci,
# whose /proc/modules check was deleted with ad0931ae26
# (its ledger row is in that commit).
#
# The probe is FORCED so the branch is reached on a host whose kernel is healthy
# (ai/rules/interop-and-goal-validation.md). The enrolment is Linux-only
# (internal/component/l2tp/pppoe/register_kernelcap_linux.go).
option=needs-linux

option=env:var=ze.test.kernelcap.force:value=pppoe=absent

tmpfs=pppoe.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
pppoe {
    enabled true
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json pppoe.conf
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-pppoe-unavailable
expect=stdout:contains=CONFIG_PPPOE
expect=stdout:contains=ze.test.kernelcap.force
